//! WP-4.1: writes the "parity" worlds used for the side-by-side checklist
//! against the real Beta 1.7.3 client (`docs/PARITY_CHECKLIST.md`).
//!
//! ```text
//! cargo run --release -p mc-golden --example parity_world -- OUT_DIR
//! ```
//!
//! Writes, through the simulation's own save path (`World::try_save_world`
//! on a `SaveOldDir`, i.e. `level.dat` + McRegion `region/*.mcr`):
//!
//! - `OUT_DIR/parity/`: a flat world (grass at y 63, dirt below, stone
//!   56-59) over chunks −8..7 × −8..7 (256 × 256 blocks, saved and marked
//!   populated; everything beyond is generated by the client from the seed)
//!   holding galleries of every block id and metadata variant this checklist
//!   looks at, a row of signs with text, three walls with every painting
//!   motive, a zoo of every mob in fenced, roofed stalls, item entities,
//!   minecarts and a boat, and five double chests holding every block item
//!   and item (for the inventory icons). The player stands at the first
//!   gallery's camera point with armour and a hotbar of items. World time
//!   6000 (noon); no rain or thunder for 500,000 ticks.
//! - `OUT_DIR/parity_nether/`: the same seed's nether around (0, 0)
//!   generated by the simulation and saved (`DIM-1/region`), the player in
//!   dimension −1 at an open spot.
//! - `OUT_DIR/views.json`: the camera points (`name`, `world`, feet `x`,
//!   `y`, `z`, `yaw`, `pitch`, `time`, `what`) that
//!   `build/screens/wp41/scripts/mkviews.py` turns into one world copy per
//!   view (only the player's position, rotation and the world time change),
//!   so that both clients load exactly the same bytes and the vanilla
//!   client needs no teleport command.
//!
//! Blocks are placed with `setBlockAndMetadata` and the metadata forced
//! again (the client's `set_block` `raw` dev path): `onBlockAdded` runs (it
//! makes tile entities and the light), the neighbours are not notified, and
//! nothing is ticked, so the shapes stay as written. Supports are placed
//! first. A few blocks change on a random tick in either client (crops and
//! saplings grow, glowing redstone ore dims, the locked chest vanishes,
//! fire ages): screenshots are taken a few seconds after loading.
//!
//! Project-owned test tooling (not vanilla code); it writes only under
//! `OUT_DIR`.

#![allow(clippy::disallowed_types, clippy::disallowed_methods)] // host tool: writes the worlds to disk

